{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:4bd0474a6898c3be","name":"H-60 Tempest Bomber","source":{"id":"source:reference-4bd0474a6898c3be","title":"H-60 Tempest Bomber","revision":19459,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:01:01Z","sha256":"90125f7dc1afce8988e02107e4c9bbdc95af8889094520bb5afbddd8358d037d","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19459","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=H-60%20Tempest%20Bomber&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-4bd0474a6898c3be","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Designed by Slayn & Korpil, the H-60 was developed in the last decades of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"}," but saw little use during that time. Its need for regular maintenance, as well as its unusual flying wing design with a cockpit at each end of the main body, made it unpopular with Republic naval planners.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Seen as a failure, small stockpiles of the ships were left in Republic scrap yards to be salvaged for parts. Many of those were illicitly sold off to independent concerns once the New Order came to power, where the bombers enjoyed moderate success for a number of years. Ultimately the design was not flexible enough to compete with more modern ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"},", though the best design elements of the H-60 were incorporated into the ",{"tag":"a","children":["B-Wing"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/B-Wing"}," designed decades later for ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Rebel Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rebel_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:52c543ff6d31425c"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Though fairly slow and lacking a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"}," (though many owners install one as an aftermarket modification), once an H-60 gets to a battle it is reasonably effective. The dual-cockpit design allows an H-60 to carry an extensive crew (with a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Copilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Copilot","referenceId":"reference:49f5b0e488cfa66c"}," behind the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"},", and a ",{"tag":"a","children":["System Operator"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/System_Operator","referenceId":"reference:75f56e8f22b64ca4"}," behind the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"},") so it can operate all systems simultaneously. The drawback to this system is the high demand for trained crews, especially compared to a ",{"tag":"a","children":["V-Wing"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/V-Wing"},". For heavy targets, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Concussion Missiles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Concussion_Missiles","referenceId":"reference:c95ee0f6eb24f16e"}," are launched while ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fire-Linked"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fire-Linked"},"; softer foes can be targeted by just one (dealing only 8d10x2 points of damage, but also using only one missile from the payload).\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Normal)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["H-60 Tempest Bomber Statistics (CL 7)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Gargantuan ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href"